.TH GOCAT-LISTEN 1 "December 2024" "GoCat 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gocat-listen \- listen for incoming connections
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gocat listen
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPORT\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Listen for incoming network connections on the specified port.
Supports TCP, UDP, SSL/TLS, and multiple concurrent connections.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exec " " \fICOMMAND\fR
Execute command for each connection
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Interactive mode
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-local
Local interactive mode
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bind " " \fIADDRESS\fR
Bind to specific address (default: 0.0.0.0)
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep\-alive
Keep connections alive
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-max\-conn " " \fICOUNT\fR
Maximum concurrent connections (default: 10)
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " " \fIDURATION\fR
Connection timeout (default: 0 = no timeout)
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-udp
Use UDP instead of TCP
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-ssl
Use SSL/TLS
.TP
.BR \-K ", " \-\-ssl\-key " " \fIFILE\fR
SSL private key file
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-ssl\-cert " " \fIFILE\fR
SSL certificate file
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Listen on port 8080:
.B gocat listen 8080
.TP
Listen with command execution:
.B gocat listen -e /bin/bash 8080
.TP
SSL listener:
.B gocat listen --ssl --ssl-cert cert.pem --ssl-key key.pem 443
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gocat (1),
.BR gocat-connect (1)
